 "title": "maths symbols",
 "source": "Symbols, scripts and layouts collected from a university linear algebra course's lecture notes (51 pages), plus a few general symbols used in homework (∃, ∖, ∘).",
 "instructions": [
  "Write each thing once in its box, the way you write maths in your notes. Blue or black pen.",
  "Sit letters on the faint dotted line. Stay inside the box; leave a box empty if unsure.",
  "√ boxes: draw the root round the dotted box with the bar just above it. Don't write inside.",
  "Print at 100 % (actual size). Photograph each page flat with all four corner squares in view."
 ],
 "footer": "Write at your normal size and speed, not neater than usual: the small differences between boxes are what make it look like you.",
